   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to direct the department of state to conduct a study on the use of\nlegal material in an electronic format and access to such legal materials",
    "basePrintNo": "S6030",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6030-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "State",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6030\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to direct the department of state to conduct a\nstudy on the use of legal material in an electronic format and access to\nsuch legal materials\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo review the manner in which electronic legal material is maintained\nand to make recommendations, if applicable, for ways to guarantee the\nauthenticity of, and continuing access to, important state legal materi-\nal.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes the department of state to study the practices for\nthe authentication, accessibility, and preservation of state legal mate-\nrial, includes guidelines for what such study should include, estab-\nlishes that the deadline for completion, submission, and public avail-\nability of the study is November 1, 2020, and provides for cooperation\nfrom relevant agencies with the department of state.\n\nSection 2 provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nProviding information online has never been more important in the opera-\ntion of state government. With the prevalence of internet access in the\n21st century, the public expects the availability and accuracy of crit-\nical materials online. The ease of creating digital materials allows\ncost-effective and timely creation and presentation of government legal\ndocuments, thereby serving the important goal s of transparency,\naccountability, and citizen participation. However, increased provision\nof this information in electronic formats, rather than in official print\nmaterials, raises the important questions of verifiable authenticity and\naccessibility.\n\nThis bill will provide for a study by the department of state to assess\nwhether action is needed to ensure the authenticity, accessibility, and\npreservation of government electronic legal materials.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2018: S6136-B; referred to Finance. 2015: S4606; referred to Finance\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
